    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt isn't only a country of pyramids."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0jfzovd6gfgj",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The "
        },
        {
          "_key": "nrornv6k6hvl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "fm23joy1j7vt"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "h06mn12eurwn",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " pyramids are overwhelming. To travel Egypt properly, you need to consider "
        },
        {
          "_key": "u8lcyuc22b94",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "3yxl1ocjld75"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "f10qoztf4or6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "srvhh7fh2qp7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "mmjni3az55ig"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "x2mvorh0bz1d",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "ddga0eld1kj9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "u6hkf5l7bruc"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "fa4wy943ue78",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", the Nile, the Red Sea, desert, oasis, and modern town life as several layers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "fm23joy1j7vt",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "3yxl1ocjld75",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "mmjni3az55ig",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "u6hkf5l7bruc",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters on first trips is not trying to see everything. Egypt is large, hot, and takes time to transfer. Packing sights doesn't strengthen impressions — it can blur them."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "On a first trip, what matters is grasping the country's shape and touring in an unstrained order."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The basic structure of Egypt travel"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Most Egypt trips build along the Nile."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "e97ezcwlblko",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "North are Cairo and Giza. Pyramids, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "4d4n622z8260",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "hb2pc0gc4rde"
          ],
          "text": "the Great Sphinx"
        },
        {
          "_key": "vg5fpfmhlgkx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Grand Egyptian Museum, Islamic Cairo, Coptic district — a city with very high ancient, medieval, and modern density."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "hb2pc0gc4rde",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.giza.the-great-sphinx",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "fwtrdv49aokz",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "South lies Luxor. The centre of ancient Thebes, gathering Karnak, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "vcd40iwpbm9f",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "mgsuewxdg5vg"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor Temple"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ydcp47pxtdas",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "vpei8snyvt7l",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "p38rawg3kh97"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Kings"
        },
        {
          "_key": "okefduir2gjh",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Hatshepsut, and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "3ozyp66aco1t",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "2l9xr1xhuipw"
          ],
          "text": "Medinet Habu"
        },
        {
          "_key": "e0p6yks0ybic",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". For deep ancient Egypt, Luxor becomes the trip's centre."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "mgsuewxdg5vg",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.the-luxor-temple",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "p38rawg3kh97",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "2l9xr1xhuipw",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.madinat-habu-temple",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "5yjh79gagmdq",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Further south is Aswan. Nile scenery calms; Nubian-culture presence thickens. Philae, Unfinished Obelisk, Nile islands, and the base for "
        },
        {
          "_key": "qpj9thawchm4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "0sagoijvi2ot"
          ],
          "text": "Abu Simbel"
        },
        {
          "_key": "cityqs5zl9s9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " further south."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "0sagoijvi2ot",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "r2ydpn2qnh7l",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan are the basic axis for first Egypt trips. With more days, you can add Red Sea, Sinai, Western Desert, or "
        },
        {
          "_key": "bhbjfcwbb3b7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "j45i5v63um1l"
          ],
          "text": "Alexandria"
        },
        {
          "_key": "4uxwv7oy1apq",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "j45i5v63um1l",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58750",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo and Giza"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Most trips start in Cairo. Cairo is Egypt's gateway and a stamina-heavy city. Traffic, sound, crowds, and city spread feel strong on first trips."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo is unmissable. The Giza pyramids and Great Sphinx let you understand Old Kingdom royal power and architectural technique with the body. Seen many times in photos, standing on the plateau, the stone size and spatial spread look different."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Grand Egyptian Museum greatly changed the meaning of Giza sightseeing. Official information includes Tutankhamun Galleries, main galleries, Grand Hall, and Khufu's boat museum in visit range. Combining pyramids and museum in the same area lets you see the ancient-Egyptian story more three-dimensionally."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6te9d3f7jgq4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Cairo, Islamic Cairo, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "y0x1ttg2cgbw",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "sv9upk9zomvz"
          ],
          "text": "Khan el-Khalili"
        },
        {
          "_key": "rie0fjxzua72",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and the Coptic district are worth time too. Leaving after only pyramids misses a lot of Cairo's long city history."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "sv9upk9zomvz",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.khan-el-khalili",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For first-timers, no need to stay too long in Cairo. Two or three nights for main places, then heading south is workable. For those easily tired by the city's strength or with children, plan car arrangement and more rest time."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To make ancient Egypt the trip's centre, allocate enough time to Luxor."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "East bank has Karnak and Luxor Temple. Karnak is a huge religious complex expanded by generations of kings. Standing in the Great Hypostyle Hall, you sense how large ancient Thebes' religious power was."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor Temple is especially impressive from evening into night. Pharaonic, Roman, Christian, and Islamic layers remain in the same space, letting you feel Egypt's layered time."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "9k9rqnw0j98h",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "West bank has Valley of the Kings, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "mer6x2xj3kcs",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "ra3qfxc1uj5q"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Queens"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ii06l4b9rlke",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Hatshepsut, Medinet Habu, and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "0ut5b3hyylvk",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "fxq5s323qe9g"
          ],
          "text": "Deir el-Medina"
        },
        {
          "_key": "lkf8thq79mmn",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". A landscape for the dead. Royal tombs, mortuary temples, and the village of those who built tombs gather on the Nile's west side."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "ra3qfxc1uj5q",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-queens",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "fxq5s323qe9g",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.deir-el-madina",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor needs at least two days, ideally three. One day works; it tends to be just transferring between sites. One day east bank, one day west bank, with margin another day west bank. Most natural on first trips."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Aswan and Abu Simbel"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Aswan feels calmer than Cairo or Luxor. The Nile surface, islands, granite rocks, Nubian villages, and slow air let you reduce trip pace."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "n054msz7rudm",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "4bt4pvvcux2g"
          ],
          "text": "Philae Temple"
        },
        {
          "_key": "krydk9janrgd",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " is known as a temple relocated to an island. With the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "xnsls197h50t",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "9t4z4d5n3e46"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan High Dam"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ot1c6rt08lel",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " construction, the UNESCO-led rescue moved Nubian sites; this is one. Beyond the temple itself, seen with modern dam construction and cultural-property protection history, meaning deepens."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "4bt4pvvcux2g",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.aswan.the-philae-temple",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "9t4z4d5n3e46",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-59236",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Unfinished Obelisk lets you understand how ancient Egyptians tried to cut huge stone. Not a finished monument but a work site stopped midway, so technique reads."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Abu Simbel sits further south from Aswan. Known for Ramesses II's great temple and Queen Nefertari's small temple, also moved through rescue work. Day trips work; with long transfer, plan with stamina and schedule margin."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Nile cruise and dahabiya"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How you move between Luxor and Aswan greatly changes the trip's character."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Most common is the Nile cruise. A larger boat over three or four nights, stopping at Edfu, Kom Ombo, and Esna en route. Transfer, lodging, food, and sightseeing combine, clear for first travellers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For quieter travel, a dahabiya — a small sailing boat — is also an option. Fewer passengers, slower, easier to make the river itself the trip's centre. Can cost more than large cruise ships; suits those who want to taste the Nile valley calmly."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "With limited time, flying or training inter-city and dropping cruise also works. Cruise is convenient, not essential. Choose by whether the trip's main purpose is sites or river time."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Red Sea and Sinai"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To not end Egypt in archaeology alone, adding the Red Sea changes the trip impression."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Sharm el-Sheikh, Dahab, Hurghada, and Marsa Alam are known as sea destinations. You can combine snorkelling, diving, and resort rest."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Around Sharm el-Sheikh, Ras Mohammed National Park and Strait of Tiran reefs are famous. Dahab is smaller and more relaxed, with sea and desert close. Hurghada combines easily with Cairo and Luxor, usable for family trips and rest."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Red Sea works well placed at the trip's end. After much walking in Cairo and Luxor, resting at the sea for two or three days keeps the whole trip from getting too heavy."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Western Desert and oases"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt has not only the Nile but a desert world."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa Oasis, near the Libyan border in the Western Desert, is known for Amazigh culture, distinct language, salt lakes, palm groves, and old mud-salt architecture. The Oracle of Amun, said visited by Alexander the Great, is also here."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Bahariya, Farafra, White Desert, and Black Desert are sometimes built into desert trips from Cairo. The White Desert shows wind-carved white limestone landform, a completely different Egypt from the Nile valley."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Desert trips need local permits, road conditions, security information, and trusted operators. Not a trip to enter deep desert on personal judgment. Confirm your government's travel information and trusted local operator judgment."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "On first Egypt trips, sometimes not packing the desert is better. For returners or itineraries of two weeks or more."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Alexandria"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Alexandria is a completely different Egypt from Cairo or Luxor. Facing the Mediterranean, a port town where Greek, Roman, Coptic, Islamic, and modern Egyptian memories layer."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The ancient great library and Pharos Lighthouse don't survive; the Qaitbay Citadel, catacombs, Roman theatre, modern Bibliotheca Alexandrina, and seaside streetscape convey the former international city's atmosphere."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For short first trips, priority can drop; with margin in Cairo, consider one night or day trip. Appealing for food, especially fish."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How many days"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "First Egypt trips vary considerably by day count."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "One week — narrowing to Cairo and Luxor is realistic. Giza, GEM, part of Cairo, Karnak, Luxor Temple, Valley of the Kings, and major west-bank sites visible."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ten days makes Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan combine easier. Including Nile cruise; Aswan to Abu Simbel with margin."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000067",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000066",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Two weeks lets you add Red Sea, Siwa, White Desert, or Alexandria. No need to add all. Even two weeks isn't enough for all of Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000069",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000068",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When planning days, don't miss transfer days. Cairo to Luxor, Luxor to Aswan, Aswan to Cairo, and Red Sea movement can each use half a day or more."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "First-trip priorities"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hard to drop on first trips: Giza pyramids, GEM, Karnak, Luxor Temple, Valley of the Kings, Hatshepsut."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Next to include: Medinet Habu, Luxor Museum, Philae, Abu Simbel, Nile cruise or dahabiya."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000070",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Add Red Sea, Siwa, White Desert, or Alexandria by trip purpose. Sea rest — Red Sea. Desert landscape — White Desert or Siwa. Mediterranean city culture — Alexandria."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000073",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000072",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters is not competing sites by count. Ancient Egypt isn't a stamp rally consuming pyramids, temples, tombs, and museums one at a time. The trip deepens as relations between eras and places become visible."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000075",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000074",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When to go"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000077",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000076",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Centring on Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan, October to April is easier travel period. Daytime temperature comparatively gentle; easier to walk outdoor sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000079",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000078",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "December and January have good climate but crowd and cost more. November, February, March balance weather and crowd."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "May to September brings harsh heat in Luxor and Aswan especially. In summer, concentrate outdoor sites in early morning; plan midday rest. For Red Sea only, summer works; consider apart from desert or inland sightseeing."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Visa, currency, safety"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Visa requirements vary by nationality and change. Egypt has official e-visa; some nationalities can use arrival visa. Before travel, confirm latest conditions on Egypt's official e-visa site, your country's Egyptian embassy, or consulate."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000081",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000080",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Currency is Egyptian pound. Hotels and some operators take foreign-currency payment; daily food, transport, tips, and small shopping need local currency. Exchange rates fluctuate; don't trust old blog figures."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000083",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000082",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For safety, Cairo, Luxor, Aswan, and Red Sea main tourist areas have long reception records. Inside Egypt, situations differ by area. For Sinai Peninsula, Western Desert, and border zones, confirm your government's travel information and use trusted operators."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000085",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000084",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Travel insurance, passport validity, emergency contacts, medication, and document copies — arrange before departure. Not over-cautious — practical to not interrupt the trip."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000087",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000086",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dress and condition management"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000089",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000088",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Egypt, heat and sun care set trip quality. Hat, sunglasses, sunscreen, light long sleeve, walking shoes — base. At sites, strong stone reflection with little shade in many places."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dress at tourist places is comparatively flexible; at religious sites, covering shoulders and knees is appropriate. Women possibly visiting mosques — carry a light scarf."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Premise tap water not being drunk. Drinking water — bottled or trusted purified; weak stomachs — care with ice and raw vegetables. Oral rehydration, regular medication, stomach medicine, and usual medication carrying reassures."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Should you use a guide"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000091",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000090",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt's major sites can be visited solo. Buying tickets, using taxis or cars, walking with maps is possible."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000093",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000092",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For first-timers, using a good guide at least part of the schedule has value. Karnak, Valley of the Kings, Giza, Islamic Cairo greatly differ in understanding with or without explanation. Wall paintings and reliefs aren't only beautiful — they were made as the language of religion, politics, and kingship."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000095",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000094",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "No need to attach a guide every day. One day in Cairo, one day on Luxor west bank — narrow to context-needing places. Museums, Corniche, felucca, and Red Sea rest days work better at your own pace."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000097",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000096",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't rush Egypt"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000099",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000098",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The most likely Egypt-trip failure is including too many sights."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Seeing pyramids and museum in Cairo, flying to Luxor the next morning, running the Valley of the Kings, moving to Aswan the next day, going to Abu Simbel, finally moving to the Red Sea. Possible on the map; in fact, quite draining."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt is a country better with some margin. Days with shortened plans for heat. Sites taking more time than expected. Stopping at the market, watching the Nile evening doing nothing — these are parts of the trip too."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For first trips, axis on Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan. With margin, add one of Red Sea or desert. That design shows Egypt best."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a1",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "No need to see all. Egypt isn't a country to finish in one trip. What matters on first trips is leaving margin that makes you want to return."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
